Two other ways that I've found of identifying the priest from outside
the temple, both involving getting the priest to do something that
generates a message:

1) Conflict.

You get messages as the high priest(ess) attacks things standing next to
him/her, and vice versa.

Possibly an abuse, although you need to get quite close to see.


2) Zap them with a wand (or other ranged attack, if there's nothing in
the way).

This will annoy them, but if it's the wrong priest, you won't need to go
any closer (and if it's the right one, a blessed scroll of taming should
calm them down).  For extra effect, stand outside the door (to avoid a
lightning zap) and use cold/fire (this will destroy a closed door,
allowing you to move through it diagonally afterwards).

Probably not an abuse, because it's quite dangerous.

